/* book Worked example 2: Q: Nitrogen is stored at 300 K and 10 MPa. For nitrogen pc = 3.39 MPa, Tc = 126.2 K, R = 0.2968 kJ/(kg·K). Find TR, pR, and estimate the specific volume v using Z from the generalized chart.
   1. TR = 300/126.2 = 2.38 and pR = 10/3.39 = 2.95.
   2. On the chart the TR = 2.4 curve sits almost exactly on Z = 1 at pR ≈ 3: read Z ≈ 1.00.
   3. v = ZRT/p = 1.00 × 0.2968 × 300/10 000 = 89.04/10 000 = 0.00890 m³/kg.
   4. Reference data give Z = 1.005 here, so the ideal-gas answer is good to about half a per cent: at this high TR the attraction and the molecular volume nearly cancel.
   Answer: TR = 2.38, pR = 2.95, Z ≈ 1.00, and v ≈ 0.00890 m³/kg. */
